From 29b667ffac148cf27df8dabb80ea64b2d30ab853 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:29:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(kernel-views): pin sysfs cpu online range and zero-cpu
 guard

### What
Pins `/sys/devices/system/cpu/online`: a single CPU renders `0\n` (no range), many CPUs render `0-(count-1)\n`, and zero CPUs fail closed with `NotFound`.

### Why it matters
The range suffix and the zero guard are boundary behavior. The existing test only reads the two-CPU case, so widening the range condition to `>= 1` or removing the zero guard survives the suite.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| `cpu_count > 1` -> `>= 1` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| remove `cpu_count == 0` guard | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-kernel-views --lib sysfs_cpu_online`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
index 37eb6517..327fa5e7 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
@@ -691,4 +691,28 @@ mod tests {
             Err(ViewError::ReadOnly)
         );
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn sysfs_cpu_online_pins_single_zero_and_range() {
+        let devices: [DeviceView; 0] = [];
+        let mut output = [0u8; 32];
+        // single cpu: "0\n" (no range suffix)
+        let one = SysFs::new(&devices, 1);
+        let len = one
+            .read(b"/sys/devices/system/cpu/online", &mut output)
+            .unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(&output[..len], b"0\n");
+        // zero cpus: NotFound (fail-closed)
+        let zero = SysFs::new(&devices, 0);
+        assert_eq!(
+            zero.read(b"/sys/devices/system/cpu/online", &mut output),
+            Err(ViewError::NotFound)
+        );
+        // many cpus: upper bound is count-1
+        let many = SysFs::new(&devices, 4);
+        let len = many
+            .read(b"/sys/devices/system/cpu/online", &mut output)
+            .unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(&output[..len], b"0-3\n");
+    }
 }
